---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Support from '../components/Support.astro';
---
<Base
  title="About"
  description="Who runs Wellness Med Care, what we publish, how we source it, and how the site is funded."
>
  <div class="wrap" style="padding-top:2.5rem">
    <div class="prose prose-center">
      <h1>About Wellness Med Care</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        We explain the administrative and financial side of American healthcare, in plain
        English, for free.
      </p>

      <h2>What we cover</h2>
      <p>
        American healthcare has two separate problems. One is clinical: what is wrong and
        what to do about it. The other is administrative: what it costs, who pays, what
        the letter in your mailbox means, and what you are allowed to push back on.
      </p>
      <p>
        Thousands of excellent sites cover the first problem, staffed by physicians and
        medical editors. Almost nobody covers the second one clearly. That is the gap we
        work in.
      </p>

      <h2>What we will never do</h2>
      <p>
        We do not interpret symptoms, suggest diagnoses, recommend treatments or
        medications, or tell you which doctor to see. We are not clinicians, and content
        that pretends otherwise does real harm. If a page here ever reads like medical
        advice, we have made a mistake - please tell us.
      </p>

      <h2>How we source things</h2>
      <p>
        Every factual claim on this site traces back to a primary source: the Centers for
        Medicare &amp; Medicaid Services, the IRS, the Department of Labor, HealthCare.gov,
        the Federal Register, or the text of the law. Those sources are listed at the
        bottom of every guide, and we link directly to them so you can check our work.
      </p>
      <p>
        Dollar amounts, contribution limits, and filing deadlines change annually. Each
        page carries a &ldquo;current as of&rdquo; date. If that date looks stale to you,
        treat the numbers as unverified and follow the source link.
      </p>

      <h2>How this is funded</h2>
      <p>
        Wellness Med Care is funded by reader donations. We plan to add ordinary display
        advertising once the site has meaningful traffic, and we may add optional paid
        features later. What we will not do is take payment from hospitals, insurers,
        billing companies, or lead buyers in exchange for coverage or placement. If that
        ever changes, it will be disclosed on this page before it happens, not after.
      </p>

      <h2>Corrections</h2>
      <p>
        If something here is wrong, out of date, or unclear, we want to know. Corrections
        are made quickly and the page date is updated when they are.
      </p>

      <Support />
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
